. sg. ऋधत्, RV.; pres. p. ऋध॑त्; cf. ऋध॑द् below) ऋध्यति;
 ऋध्नोति;
 ऋणद्धि;
 आनर्ध, अर्धिता, अर्धिष्यति, &c., to grow, increase, prosper, succeed, RV.; AV.; ŚBr.; MBh.; Mn. &c.;
to cause to increase or prosper, promote, make prosperous, accomplish, RV.; AV.; VS.; ŚBr. :
Pass. ऋध्यते, to be promoted, increase, prosper, succeed, ŚBr.; BṛĀrUp. :
Caus. अर्धयति, to satisfy, AV. vii, 80, 4; Nir. :
Desid. अर्दिधिषति or ईर्त्सति;
 [cf. √ राध् and वृध्.]
